# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ferry — Environment Configuration (Stellar Testnet)
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and adjust as needed.
# Never commit `.env.local` or any file containing real secrets.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Stellar network (Testnet only for this project)
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK=TESTNET
NEXT_PUBLIC_HORIZON_URL=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org
NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE="Test SDF Network ; September 2015"

# Home domain of this application, presented to anchors during
# SEP-10 Web Authentication (must match the domain Ferry is served from).
NEXT_PUBLIC_HOME_DOMAIN=localhost:3000

# Default test anchor used for SEP-24 / SEP-31 / SEP-38 flows.
# The anchor's home domain must expose /.well-known/stellar.toml (SEP-1)
# with WEB_AUTH_ENDPOINT, TRANSFER_SERVER_SEP0024, DIRECT_PAYMENT_SERVER
# and ANCHOR_QUOTE_SERVER entries.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANCHOR_DOMAIN=testanchor.stellar.org

# Base URL of this app (used for server-side API route calls, callbacks, etc.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Comma-separated domains the server will resolve/proxy at all (SSRF
# guard) — server-only, not NEXT_PUBLIC. Defaults to testanchor.stellar.org
# if unset. To run the EUR(EURC)->TRY corridor against the local mock
# anchor (mock-anchor/ — see its README, since no public TRY-issuing
# anchor exists on Testnet), set this to include localhost:4001 and set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANCHOR_DOMAIN=localhost:4001 above. See docs/RUNBOOK.md §2.
# ANCHOR_ALLOWLIST=testanchor.stellar.org,localhost:4001

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Embedded mock anchor (app/api/mock-anchor/*, app/.well-known/stellar.toml)
# Runs the same TRY-leg mock as mock-anchor/ inside THIS Next.js app, so it
# actually works on Vercel — unlike mock-anchor/'s own standalone Express
# process, which Vercel has nowhere to host. Use this when
# testanchor.stellar.org's SEP-31 endpoint is unavailable/broken (see
# GAP_ANALYSIS.md) and you don't want to run mock-anchor/ separately.
# See docs/RUNBOOK.md's embedded-mock-anchor section for the full picture.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to "true" to make this deployment resolve anchor requests against its
# own /api/mock-anchor/* routes instead of an external anchor. Leaving
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANCHOR_DOMAIN unset then makes ANCHOR_DOMAIN default to this
# deployment's own domain (NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL, or Vercel's own VERCEL_URL)
# instead of testanchor.stellar.org — and that domain is auto-added to the
# allowlist above, so no separate ANCHOR_ALLOWLIST edit is needed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_EMBEDDED_MOCK_ANCHOR=true

# Server-only equivalent of the flag above (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so it's
# never bundled client-side). Either one alone is sufficient — set this
# instead of the NEXT_PUBLIC_ variant if you'd rather the flag not be
# visible in client-side JS. lib/stellar/anchorAllowlist.ts and
# lib/stellar/config.ts check both and treat "true" on either as enabled.
# ENABLE_EMBEDDED_MOCK_ANCHOR=true

# The embedded mock anchor's own Testnet identity — a SEP-10 signing key
# (which doubles as the EURC-receiving settlement account) and a TRY-issuer
# key, server-only secrets (never NEXT_PUBLIC_). Leave unset for local
# `npm run dev` — a fresh keypair is generated and Friendbot-funded
# automatically. On Vercel, PIN both explicitly: an unset secret falls back
# to a random keypair generated once per warm serverless instance, which is
# NOT the same key across cold starts / multiple instances, and SEP-10
# requires the anchor's signing key to stay stable across the
# challenge-issue and challenge-verify requests. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('@stellar/stellar-sdk').Keypair.random().secret())"
# then fund the resulting public key via https://friendbot.stellar.org.
# MOCK_ANCHOR_SIGNING_SECRET=
# MOCK_ANCHOR_TRY_ISSUER_SECRET=

# Signs the embedded mock anchor's own SEP-10 JWTs. Leave unset for local
# dev; set to a real random value before treating a deployment as
# demo-ready — an unset value uses a fixed, publicly-known dev default.
# MOCK_ANCHOR_JWT_SECRET=

# Override the EURC / mock-TRY asset issuers used to build SEP-38/31 asset
# identifiers. Leave unset to use Circle's real, verified Testnet EURC
# issuer and this repo's default mock TRY issuer — see
# CORRIDOR_VERIFICATION.md §5 before changing either.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EURC_ISSUER=GB3Q6QDZYTHWT7E5PVS3W7FUT5GVAFC5KSZFFLPU25GO7VTC3NM2ZTVO
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_TRY_ISSUER=GADBO465IHRW3WNOCNM7H5UEXKER4TGT2FSBYUDHMKFOAYR2YHAQ72FZ

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Security note: Ferry is strictly non-custodial. It never stores,
# requests, or transmits private keys / secret seeds. All signing
# happens client-side via the Freighter wallet extension.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
